\title{\textbf{A 1.5\,V, 50\,mA PMOS Low-Dropout Regulator in 0.18\,$\mu$m CMOS}\\[0.4ex]
\large Part 2: Hand calculation of $W/L$ from the specification, and ngspice verification}
\date{November 2026}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
\noindent
This note sizes a PMOS low-dropout regulator from a written specification and checks it in ngspice.
Section~\ref{sec:models} extracts square-law parameters from the 0.18\,$\mu$m BSIM3 model.
Section~\ref{sec:hand} computes every $W/L$, bias current and resistor step by step. Section~\ref{sec:sim}
verifies the design, reports three iterations, explains each gap between hand calculation and
simulation, and lists the corner results. The final design meets every specification at the nominal point.
\textbf{All equation, lemma, proposition and corollary numbers refer to Part~1}
(\texttt{ldo\_theory\_proofs.pdf}), where each formula is proved; tables, figures and sections refer to this note.
\end{abstract}

\tableofcontents

