\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.82\textwidth]{figures/gm_over_id.png}
\caption{Simulated $g_m/I_D$ versus current density. The square law predicts $g_m/I_D = 2/\ov$, which
is 20\,V$^{-1}$ at $\ov = 0.1$\,V. The real device gives about 17\,V$^{-1}$ there (moderate inversion) and
levels off near $1/(nV_T)\approx 26$\,V$^{-1}$ in weak inversion; this is one source of the hand-versus-simulation gap in Section~\ref{sec:gap}.}
