\paragraph{Note on the model file.} ngspice reports that the model parameters \texttt{XL} and \texttt{XW} are not recognised and ignores
them. In this file $XL = 0$ and $XW = -10$\,nm, so the effect is a 10\,nm width change and is negligible
for the widths used here.


%===================================================================================
\section{Hand design from the specification}\label{sec:hand}
The script \texttt{design.py} carries out the steps below; each number is quoted from its output. This
section describes the final design (v3). Section~\ref{sec:iter} explains how v1 and v2 led to it.

\paragraph{Step 1 -- Divider.} $\beta = \VREF/\VOUT = <<H['beta']|.2f>>$. A divider current
$I_{div} = <<H['I_div']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$A gives $R_2 = \VREF/I_{div} = <<H['R2']/1e3|.0f>>$\,k$\Omega$ and
$R_1 = (\VOUT-\VREF)/I_{div} = <<H['R1']/1e3|.0f>>$\,k$\Omega$.

\paragraph{Step 2 -- Pass device.} Eq.~\eqref{T-eq:wl_sat} with $\KP = <<P['p_L0.18']['KP']*1e6|.1f>>\,\mu$A/V$^2$ (PMOS,
$L = 0.18\,\mu$m) and $V_{IN,nom}-\VOUT = 0.3$\,V (10\,mV margin) gives $W/L \ge <<2*SP['IL_MAX']/(P['p_L0.18']['KP']*0.29**2)|.0f>>$. Rounding up
to $<<H['MP']|d>>$ fingers of 10\,$\mu$m gives $W = <<H['WP']*1e3|.1f>>$\,mm and $W/L = <<H['WL_p']|.0f>>$. Then:
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=0.1ex]
\item Full load: $\ov = <<H['vov_p']*1e3|.0f>>$\,mV, $\VSGP = <<H['vsg_max_load']|.3f>>$\,V,
$\gmP = 2I/\ov = <<H['gm_p_max']|.3f>>$\,S.
\item Dropout check \eqref{T-eq:vov_do} at $V_{DO} = <<SP['VDO']|.1f>>$\,V: $\ov = <<H['vov_do']*1e3|.0f>>$\,mV, i.e.\
$\VSGP^{DO} = <<H['vsg_do']|.3f>>$\,V, which the drive chain can reach (Step 6).
\item Light load ($<<SP['IL_MIN']*1e3|.1f>>$\,mA, weak inversion): the square law does not apply, so
$\VSGP = <<H['vsg_min_load']|.3f>>$\,V and $\gmP = <<H['gm_p_min']*1e3|.2f>>$\,mS are read from the simulated
$I_D$--$V_{SG}$ curve of one finger. Hence $\Delta\VSGP = <<H['dVSG']*1e3|.0f>>$\,mV.
\item Gate capacitance: $C_G = \tfrac23WLC_{ox} + 2WC_{ov} = <<H['Cg']*1e12|.2f>>$\,pF.
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Step 3 -- Required loop gain $G = \beta\Aea\Ab$.} Each specification gives a lower bound
on $G$:
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=0.1ex]
\item PSRR (Proposition~\ref{T-prop:psrr}): $G \ge 10^{30/20} = <<H['G_psrr']|.1f>>$.
\item Load regulation (Corollary~\ref{T-cor:static}b): $G \ge \Delta\VSGP/15\,\text{mV} = <<H['G_load']|.1f>>$.
\item Line regulation (Corollary~\ref{T-cor:static}c): $G \ge 1/(35\,\text{mV/V}) = <<H['G_line']|.1f>>$.
\end{itemize}
The binding one is the PSRR: $G \ge <<H['G_req']|.1f>>$, i.e.\ $\Aea\Ab \ge <<H['G_req']/H['beta']|.0f>>$.

\paragraph{Step 4 -- Error amplifier gain.} $\Aea = (2/V_{OV1})/(\lambda_p+\lambda_n)$ with $V_{OV1} = <<V3['vov1']|.2f>>$\,V,
$L_{12} = <<V3['L12']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$m and $L_{34} = <<V3['L34']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$m:
$\lambda_p+\lambda_n = <<V3['lam_sum']|.3f>>$\,V$^{-1}$, so $\Aea = <<V3['A_ea']|.0f>>$
(<<db(V3['A_ea'])|.1f>>\,dB). Buffer at $I_B = <<V3['I_B']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$A: $\Ab = <<V3['A_b']|.3f>>$. Hence
$G = <<V3['G']|.1f>>$ (<<db(V3['G'])|.1f>>\,dB), which is above the requirement.

\paragraph{Step 5 -- Unity-gain frequency and poles.}
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=0.1ex]
\item Eq.~\eqref{T-eq:fu} at full load: $\fu = <<V3['UGF_max']/1e6|.2f>>$\,MHz.
\item Buffer pole: $g_{mB} = 2I_B/V_{OV,B} = <<V3['gm_b']*1e3|.2f>>$\,mS, so $p_B = <<V3['p_b']/1e6|.1f>>$\,MHz.
\item EA output capacitance: $C_{EA} = <<V3['C_ea']*1e15|.0f>>$\,fF, of which $M_2$ contributes <<V3['cparts']['c_m2']*1e15|.0f>>\,fF.
With $R_{o,EA} = <<V3['Ro_ea']/1e3|.0f>>$\,k$\Omega$ this gives $p_{EA} = <<V3['p_ea']/1e6|.2f>>$\,MHz.
\item ESR zero at $\RESR = 10$\,m$\Omega$: $z_{ESR} = <<V3['z_esr']/1e6|.1f>>$\,MHz.
\end{itemize}
Evaluating the full transfer function \eqref{T-eq:T} numerically gives PM $= <<V3['heavy']['PM']|.0f>>^\circ$ at
full load ($<<V3['heavy_esr0']['PM']|.0f>>^\circ$ with $\RESR = 0$) and $<<V3['light']['PM']|.0f>>^\circ$ at
light load. The hand PM with $\RESR = 0$ sits right at the 45$^\circ$ limit, and the ESR bound \eqref{T-eq:esr},
$<<V3['ESR_bound']*1e3|.0f>>$\,m$\Omega$, is slightly below the 50\,m$\Omega$ end of the range. Both are
pessimistic: the bound is only sufficient, and the hand $G$ is too high (Section~\ref{sec:gap}). The simulation
(Fig.~\ref{fig:psrr}, right) decides.

\paragraph{Step 6 -- EA current and buffer $V_{SG}$.} By Proposition~\ref{T-prop:pea}, the EA current
does not move $p_{EA}$, so it is set by the power budget: $I_{D1} = <<V3['I_D1']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$A per side. The
window \eqref{T-eq:window} gives
$<<H['vsgb_lo']|.3f>>\,\text{V} \le \VSGB \le <<H['vsgb_hi']|.3f>>$\,V. Its centre,
<<H['vsgb_mid']|.3f>>\,V, sets $V_{OV,B} = <<V3['vov_b']|.2f>>$\,V.

\paragraph{Step 7 -- Predictions and current budget.}
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=0.1ex]
\item Load regulation $\Delta\VSGP/G = <<V3['loadreg']*1e3|.1f>>$\,mV.
\item Line regulation $1/G = <<V3['linereg']*1e3|.1f>>$\,mV/V.
\item $\mathrm{PSRR}_{DC} = <<V3['psrr_dc_dB']|.1f>>$\,dB.
\item $I_Q = I_{REF} + 2I_{D1} + I_B + I_{div} = <<V3['Iq']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$A.
\end{itemize}

