\caption{Load step. The step-up settles within 1\,mV immediately (fast loop at full load). The release
settles exponentially with a fitted $\tau = <<TAU*1e6|.1f>>\,\mu$s, against
$1/(2\pi f_{u,light}) = <<1/(2*pi*FU_LIGHT)*1e6|.1f>>\,\mu$s from Proposition~\ref{T-prop:step}. There is no overshoot, as the
single-pole model predicts. The total excursion, <<S3['tran']['dip_from_initial']*1e3|.1f>>\,mV, is almost all the static
load regulation (<<S3['loadreg']['dV']*1e3|.1f>>\,mV).}
